A||||11||Bill Osmer||Received Rodney's new front struts||||14||
Z||000000||Bill Osmer||08-07-2001||01:28 PM||||Today, I came home from the office to a long box (a delivery from Rodney Dickman) begging me to open it.<BR>When I did, I found inside 2 substantial metal mounting brackets and a LONG pressurized cylinder. I couldn't wait to see how they assembled to my Fiero. In less than 10 minutes, I was able to remove my old support strut (it only takes a 10mm socket wrench!), and replaced it with Rodney's new front hood strut. (NOTE: Rodney - you may want to generate a paragraph of installation instructions, although I had absolutely no problems). <BR>Once installed, the new support strut worked GREAT - not really a surprise. The front hood now raises easily, stays in place when raised and lowers without having to operate a finicky latch (I always forgot about the 2nd stop!). It seems to be the making of another fine Rodney Dickman product. <BR> <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Image018_3.jpg">   <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Image016_1.jpg"> <P><BR>------------------<BR>Bill Osmer<BR>                <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forumcardsig2.jpg">                <BR><p>[This message has been edited by Bill Osmer (edited 08-07-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000001||Leadfoot||08-07-2001||02:14 PM||||Now I have to revise my x-mas list:<P>1) broom stick to hold front lid (scratched!)<BR>1) front strut assembly<BR>1) 3.4L engine<P>Looks good.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">||||reg||1
